 ## Logging (`src/logger.ts`)
 
-The logger writes one JSON line to stdout per call, with `level`, `message`, any extra fields and a timestamp. Its fields can only be strings, numbers or booleans. None of `users.ts`, `orders.ts` or `db.ts` logs anything at the moment.
+The logger writes one JSON line to stdout per call, with `level`, `message`, any extra fields and a timestamp. Its fields can only be strings, numbers or booleans. Only `createUser` logs at the moment; `orders.ts`, `db.ts` and the other user functions do not.
+
+`createUser` logs one line per outcome:
+
+| Level | Message | Fields |
+|---|---|---|
+| `info` | `createUser succeeded` | `userId` |
+| `warn` | `createUser rejected: invalid input` | `reason` (the validation message, which names the field but not the value) |
+| `warn` | `createUser rejected: email already registered` | `existingUserId` (the id of the account that already owns the email) |
+| `error` | `createUser failed: email lookup error` / `insert error` | `errorName` (class name only, since db error messages could contain user data) |
+
+A user who fails sign-up has no id yet, so failures other than the duplicate email cannot be tied to a person.
 
 Project rules in `CLAUDE.md` apply when logging is added:
 
